{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_21\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 10B #21</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems#Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 12B #19</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Regular polygons with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cf9c5ca516b05bd21084f414edb7a9ee01642b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,6,7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides are inscribed in the same circle. No two of the polygons share a vertex, and no three of their sides intersect at a common point. At how many points inside the circle do two of their sides intersect?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28e2ecf8fb3ca7da3b050495ed67c38a66a1389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\textbf{A})\\: 52\\qquad(\\textbf{B}) \\: 56\\qquad(\\textbf{C}) \\: 60\\qquad(\\textbf{D}) \\: 64\\qquad(\\textbf{E}) \\: 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"385\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Imagine we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> regular polygons with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c1867cd31fa2542f75b0c24655922d93ce901d81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" /> inscribed in a circle without sharing a vertex. We see that each side of the polygon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides (the polygon with fewer sides) will be intersected twice.\n(We can see this because to have a vertex of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />-gon on an arc subtended by a side of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon, there will be one intersection to “enter” the arc and one to “exit” the arc. ~KingRavi)\n</p><p>This means that we will end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the number of sides in the polygon with fewer sides.\n</p><p>If we have polygons with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d376878680af5f19b8b3860db9417f29950094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43420adcd0fce9dce3978d53b97a8e0262b58da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides, we need to consider each possible pair of polygons and count their intersections. \n</p><p>Throughout <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these pairs, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided polygon has the least number of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided polygon has the least number of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided polygon has the least number of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> time.\n</p><p>Therefore the number of intersections is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03934ecd471a91d07ccd646ccf4d069c70e9729d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot(3\\cdot5+2\\cdot6+1\\cdot7)=\\boxed{(\\textbf{E}) \\:68}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"261\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For regular polygons with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cf9c5ca516b05bd21084f414edb7a9ee01642b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,6,7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> points of intersection inside the circle are shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4500ea46f17a2a9e504f378cf977b69c4ad590d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */  size(350); path p5 = polygon(5); path p6 = polygon(6); path p7 = rotate(180)*polygon(7); path p8 = polygon(8);  draw(p5,red); draw(p6,green); draw(p7,blue); draw(p8,olive);  draw(Circle(origin,1));  dot(intersectionpoints(p5,p6),linewidth(2.5)); dot(intersectionpoints(p5,p7),linewidth(2.5)); dot(intersectionpoints(p5,p8),linewidth(2.5)); dot(intersectionpoints(p6,p7),linewidth(2.5)); dot(intersectionpoints(p6,p8),linewidth(2.5)); dot(intersectionpoints(p7,p8),linewidth(2.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"585\" height=\"585\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7cfZwwYSttQ\">https://youtu.be/7cfZwwYSttQ</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution 2 by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5nHMBfDyvps\">https://youtu.be/5nHMBfDyvps</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yTQSKinIo8g\">https://youtu.be/yTQSKinIo8g</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><s